From my subjective viewpoint, [er] [e=C9=BE] [e=CA=81] are easier to hear t=
han
[e=C9=B9]. [=C9=B9] sounds to me the most vowel-ish among them and tends to
blend into the surrounding vowel rather than cutting it out. If I
wanted to make a clearer distinction between "e" and "ei" in speech by
/r/, I would use [r] or [=CA=81].


